From d957ca89296f0cb16a27b59be0fcf111266d8ba6 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: maolo80 <maolo80@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 23 Oct 2026 16:38:15 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 1/3] TeknoNaomi: expose cabinet outputs, free play, BIOS,
 precise FPU and VR

The TeknoNaomi runner already accepts --outputs, --free-play, --bios,
--sh4-precise-fpu, --sbs and the --vr family, but TPUI offered none of
them. Normalize now adds the fields to stock and saved profiles alike,
and the launch plan validates and passes them.

Release checks cover the defaults, each option, VR precedence over
side-by-side and rejection of invalid BIOS, VR size and filter values.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01Xkm42Nb8k8qCUfB5RCiVU3
